From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d012 setup <setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] A ws:// address reaches the ad hoc relay through a local bridge

An ad hoc server address that starts with ws:// is a relay that is only reachable over WebSocket (a Cloudflare Worker). A bridge inside the process listens on 127.0.0.1 ports 27312 and 27313 and forwards each connection, byte for byte, to ws://host/ctl and ws://host/relay in binary frames; the client talks to the bridge unchanged. The bridge is generic: a table of local port and path, so another service can use it. Nothing changes for an address without the ws:// prefix.
---

